
title: Merchant
---
<<declare $metMerchant = false>>
<<if $metMerchant == false>>
    Merchant: Welcome, traveller!
    Merchant: First time visiting my little shop?
    {$playerName}: You have a shop here?
    Merchant: Of course!
    Merchant: Even in a place as strange as this, people need supplies.
    {$playerName}: You don't seem particularly worried about being stuck here.
    Merchant: Oh, believe me, I am.
    Merchant: But worrying won't put food on the table.
    Merchant: Besides, if we're going to be stuck here, we might as well make the best of it!
    {$playerName}: I suppose that's one way to look at things.
    Merchant: Exactly!
    Merchant: Now then, looking to buy something, or perhaps sell a few things?
    <<set $metMerchant = true>>
<<else>>
    Merchant: Welcome back, traveller!
    Merchant: Looking to buy something, or perhaps sell a few things?
<<endif>>
-> Buy Items
    Merchant: Of course! Take a look at what I've got.
    <<jump MerchantBuy>>
-> Sell Items
    Merchant: Let's see what you've got to sell.
    <<jump MerchantSell>>
-> Ask about this place
    {$playerName}: Do you know anything about where we are?
    Merchant: Unfortunately, not much.
    Merchant: One moment I was sorting through my supplies.
    Merchant: The next, I woke up in this strange place.
    Merchant: Floating islands, unusual creatures, and people appearing out of nowhere...
    Merchant: Certainly not what I expected when I woke up this morning!
    {$playerName}: And you're still running a shop?
    Merchant: Of course!
    Merchant: Adventurers still need supplies.
    Merchant: And I happen to have plenty!
    Merchant: Now, is there anything I can help you with?
    <<jump Merchant>>
-> Leave
    {$playerName}: Nothing for now.
    Merchant: Safe travels!
===
title: MerchantBuy
---
Merchant: What are you looking for?
-> Buy Health Potion - 25 gold
    <<if can_buy_item("health_potion")>>
        {$playerName}: I'll take a Health Potion.
        Merchant: A wise choice!
        Merchant: You never know when you might need one.
        <<buy_item GameManager "health_potion">>
        Merchant: Here you go. One Health Potion!
        Merchant: Anything else catch your eye?
    <<else>>
        Merchant: Sorry, you either don't have enough gold or your inventory is full.
        Merchant: A Health Potion costs 25 gold.
    <<endif>>
    <<jump MerchantBuy>>
-> Buy Gem - 50 gold
    <<if can_buy_item("gem")>>
        {$playerName}: How much for that gem?
        Merchant: 50 gold.
        Merchant: Quite a pretty little thing, isn't it?
        {$playerName}: I'll take it.
        <<buy_item GameManager "gem">>
        Merchant: Excellent choice!
        Merchant: Just be careful who you show it to.
        Merchant: Some people have a habit of making valuables disappear.
    <<else>>
        Merchant: Sorry, you either don't have enough gold or your inventory is full.
        Merchant: That gem costs 50 gold.
    <<endif>>
    <<jump MerchantBuy>>
-> Buy Apple - 10 gold
    <<if can_buy_item("apple")>>
        {$playerName}: I'd like to buy an apple.
        Merchant: Ah, something simple for a change!
        Merchant: That'll be 10 gold.
        <<buy_item GameManager "apple">>
        Merchant: Here you go! One fresh apple.
        Merchant: Well, as fresh as anything can be around here.
    <<else>>
        Merchant: Sorry, you either don't have enough gold or your inventory is full.
        Merchant: An apple costs 10 gold.
    <<endif>>
    <<jump MerchantBuy>>
-> Buy Mana Potion - 30 gold
    <<if can_buy_item("mana_potion")>>
        {$playerName}: I'd like to buy a Mana Potion.
        Merchant: A Mana Potion?
        Merchant: Planning on practising some magic?
        {$playerName}: It's for someone who needs it.
        Merchant: Ah, I see!
        Merchant: Well, you're in luck.
        Merchant: That'll be 30 gold.
        <<buy_item GameManager "mana_potion">>
        Merchant: Here you go! One Mana Potion.
        Merchant: Hopefully it'll help whoever you're buying it for.
    <<else>>
        Merchant: Sorry, you either don't have enough gold or your inventory is full.
        Merchant: A Mana Potion costs 30 gold.
    <<endif>>
    <<jump MerchantBuy>>
-> Go back
    <<jump Merchant>>
===
title: MerchantSell
---
Merchant: What are you looking to sell?
-> Sell Gem - 35 gold
    <<if can_sell_item("gem")>>
        {$playerName}: I've got this gem. Interested?
        Merchant: Oh, that's a lovely little gem!
        Merchant: I'll give you 35 gold for it.
        {$playerName}: Sounds fair.
        <<sell_item GameManager "gem">>
        Merchant: Pleasure doing business with you!
    <<else>>
        Merchant: Sorry, you don't have a Gem that I can buy.
    <<endif>>
    <<jump MerchantSell>>
-> Sell Health Potion - 10 gold
    <<if can_sell_item("health_potion")>>
        {$playerName}: I'd like to sell this Health Potion.
        Merchant: Certainly!
        Merchant: I'll give you 10 gold for it.
        <<sell_item GameManager "health_potion">>
        Merchant: Thank you!
        Merchant: Anything else you'd like to sell?
    <<else>>
        Merchant: You don't have any Health Potions to sell.
    <<endif>>
    <<jump MerchantSell>>
-> Sell Apple - 5 gold
    <<if can_sell_item("apple")>>
        {$playerName}: I've got an apple. Would you be interested?
        Merchant: An apple? Certainly!
        Merchant: I'll give you 5 gold for it.
        {$playerName}: Sounds fair.
        <<sell_item GameManager "apple">>
        Merchant: Pleasure doing business with you!
        Merchant: Anything else you'd like to sell?
    <<else>>
        Merchant: Sorry, you don't have any apples to sell.
    <<endif>>
    <<jump MerchantSell>>
-> Sell Mana Potion - 12 gold
    <<if can_sell_item("mana_potion")>>
        {$playerName}: I'd like to sell this Mana Potion.
        Merchant: A Mana Potion?
        Merchant: Those are always useful for adventurers.
        Merchant: I'll give you 12 gold for it.
        {$playerName}: Deal.
        <<sell_item GameManager "mana_potion">>
        Merchant: Pleasure doing business with you!
        Merchant: Anything else?
    <<else>>
        Merchant: You don't have any Mana Potions to sell.
    <<endif>>
    <<jump MerchantSell>>
-> Never mind
    {$playerName}: Actually, I'll hold onto my things.
    <<jump Merchant>>
===
